            <ArticleTitle>Multiple cranial nerve palsies as the presenting features of prostate carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>194-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1440-1673.2008.01943.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cranial nerve palsies have previously been reported in metastatic prostate carcinoma, usually occurring late in the course of the disease. We describe the case of a 55-year-old man whose diagnosis of prostate cancer was made following investigation of multiple cranial nerve palsies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
